[0.552, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\r\u001b[2C\u001b[6B\u001b[48;2;55;55;55m\u001b[38;2;255;255;255mL35-L50: I confirm them all\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BDelete the leftover empty folders.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BTote pricing must be set by it's actual weight. Fix weights that are incorrect. There is data available for packing \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bdensity and weight / density of all the items so you can work out the weight of a tote with any given item.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BWhich development sandbox? If there is one in jettison, then probably yes, and each project builds it's own sandbox \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bas needed. Jettison should only provide structure, support, code, for common features or features that are exclusive \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bto jettison and not expected to be overridden by manifest and other games.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BSet validation to 30 times now, but that does seem like a massive amount of price inflation so schedule a task to \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bevaluate what is causing it and if it should stay at that value.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BRemind me to review those number once the next steps are done.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[2BJettison should provide an interface for dock control that allows a game to determine and create it's own rules for \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Badmission, refusal, rank, etc. It should be game agnostic, just supplying the core functions.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[2B\u001b[49m\u001b[38;2;215;119;87mSlithering\u001b[38;2;235;159;127m…\u001b[20G\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m8\u001b[39m\u001b[27;1H\u001b[24;3H\u001b[?25h"]
