48;248;242m></a>L51 | Price inflation: the hosted multipliers reach about 27 times an\u001b[105Git\u001b[108Gm's ba\r\u001b[9C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mse price,\u001b[22Gso `IsValidBasePrice`'s\u001b[46Groom\u001b[51Gwas\u001b[55Graised\u001b[62Gfrom\u001b[67G10\u001b[70Gto\u001b[73G30\u001b[76Gtimes\u001b[82Gon\u001b[85G2026-11-25.\u001b[97GFind\u001b[102Gwhat\u001b[107Gdrives\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m     +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242ma price that high (the native curve, scarcity, the local bias, or a fault), and whether 30 stays. **Do\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m     +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mne when** the cause is named, the bound is set to what the multipliers can reach, and a test pins the \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m     +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mhighest. | — | [\u001b[38;2;230;219;116mPrices\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m](pricing.md#limits-and-open-work) |                                            \r\u001b[2C\u001b[2B\u001b[39m\u001b[49mR\u001b[6Gding \u001b[1m1\u001b[14G\u001b[22mile…\u001b[19G\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m$ t\u001b[10Gil -c 600 '/home/iv\u001b[30Gn/projects/manifest/docs/delivery-order.md'\r\u001b[18C\u001b[8B(shift+tab to cycle)\u001b[39m\u001b[27;1H\u001b[21;3H\u001b[?25h"]
